Description: GNOME Shell extension: per-monitor lock screen, clock and weather
 Gives the GNOME Shell lock screen a wallpaper per monitor with blur and dim,
 its own clock layout, and the current weather with an animated icon. The
 weather comes from Open-Meteo for a place you choose in the preferences; the
 extension never looks your location up by itself.
 .
 After installing, log out and back in once, then enable it with
 `gnome-extensions enable lock-screen-suite@spencercnorton.github.io`.
